From b9a68305499a8a54508842b7fe5b4286a43a893c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Ewing <marc@riotracing.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:42:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libFLAC: Ogg decoder, return what we have instead of waiting
 for more

The Ogg read callback wrapper fills the whole request before returning:
when no complete page is buffered it asks the client for more data, even
when it already has bytes to hand back. libFLAC's bitreader requests up to
its capacity (8 KiB) and takes partial reads, so the wait gains nothing,
but on a live stream it can last a long time. Near-silence encodes to a
few hundred bytes a second, so a player that tunes in while a stream is
quiet gets no samples until 8 KiB has arrived, then plays from the start
of what it buffered and stays that far behind for as long as it listens.

Measured with MPD 0.24.15 (which decodes Ogg FLAC through libFLAC) on a
stream paced page by page in real time, 48 kHz near-silence: it started
playing after 12 s and stayed 12 s behind; with this change it plays
about two pages behind (2 s with 1 s pages, 1 s with 0.25 s pages).

On a live Icecast stream (ffmpeg, 0.256 s pages, about 300 bytes a second
while near-silent), MPD that connected while the stream was quiet played
nothing for the 40 s it stayed quiet, then 40 s behind once audio came.
With this change it played 0.3 s behind throughout.

Return once there is something to return and no complete page is
buffered; read from the client only when there is nothing to return yet.
Decoding files is unchanged except that some reads return less.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016rSr6RyB719BULhakT1QHf
---
 src/libFLAC/ogg_decoder_aspect.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libFLAC/ogg_decoder_aspect.c b/src/libFLAC/ogg_decoder_aspect.c
index ae9649a..296186e 100644
--- a/src/libFLAC/ogg_decoder_aspect.c
+++ b/src/libFLAC/ogg_decoder_aspect.c
@@ -333,7 +333,11 @@ FLAC__OggDecoderAspectReadStatus FLAC__ogg_decoder_aspect_read_callback_wrapper(
 	 * pages down to libFLAC in such a way that we obey its size
 	 * requirement.  To limit the amount of callbacks, we will always try
 	 * to read in enough pages to return the full number of bytes
-	 * requested.
+	 * requested, except that once we have something to return, we return
+	 * it rather than ask the client for more.  On a live stream that next
+	 * read can wait a long time (near-silence encodes to a few hundred
+	 * bytes a second, so filling an 8 KiB request can take tens of
+	 * seconds), and libFLAC takes partial reads.
 	 */
 	*bytes = 0;
 	while (*bytes < bytes_requested && !aspect->end_of_stream) {
@@ -430,7 +434,11 @@ FLAC__OggDecoderAspectReadStatus FLAC__ogg_decoder_aspect_read_callback_wrapper(
 			}
 			else if (ret == 0) {
 				/* need more data */
-				FLAC__OggDecoderAspectReadStatus status = read_more_data_(aspect, read_callback, bytes_requested - *bytes, decoder, client_data);
+				FLAC__OggDecoderAspectReadStatus status;
+				/* but first return what we have, see above */
+				if(*bytes > 0)
+					return FLAC__OGG_DECODER_ASPECT_READ_STATUS_OK;
+				status = read_more_data_(aspect, read_callback, bytes_requested - *bytes, decoder, client_data);
 				if(status != FLAC__OGG_DECODER_ASPECT_READ_STATUS_OK)
 					return status;
 			}
